# behavioral-regression gate — enforcement sentinel (#5864)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the behavioural-regression pass-rate gate
# (.github/workflows/behavioral-regression.yml) BLOCKS or merely REPORTS when the
# corpus at core/disciplines/evals/behavioral-regression/ scores below the floor
# recorded at [behavioral_regression].pass_rate_floor.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token:
#   warn      → report only (exit 0); a below-floor verdict is surfaced but does not block.
#   enforce   → block on a below-floor verdict at the major-release boundary (exit 1).
#
# THE TOKEN IS ONE OF THREE CONJUNCTS, NOT THE WHOLE PREDICATE. The gate blocks iff:
#     sentinel == "enforce"  AND  context == a v*.00 tag  AND  the runner exits non-zero
# Flipping this token alone does NOT make the advisory pull-request rung blocking —
# that rung is non-blocking by construction in the workflow itself, and making it block
# is a separate, later decision that edits the workflow's predicate. Nor does flipping
# it make the gate a required check: branch protection is repository settings, lives
# out of tree, and no committed file can assert membership in it. Both remaining steps
# are named below because a graduation clause that names only the token is incomplete,
# and whoever performs the flip reads THIS file rather than the standard.
#
# TWO STEPS TO GRADUATE, NOT THREE. The sibling release-corpus-completeness gate carries
# a third step — delete the paths: filter — because a path-filtered context registered
# in branch protection leaves every non-matching pull request permanently PENDING. This
# gate ships FILTER-FREE from day one (always-reports=yes), so that step does not exist
# here. What remains:
#   1. Flip the token below to `enforce`.
#   2. Add the "Behavioral-regression pass-rate gate" job to required_status_checks.
#
# EXIT CRITERION FOR THE SHAKEDOWN — EVALUABLE FROM COMMITTED STATE, so the decision to
# flip never depends on a git-ignored log nobody can read back:
#   (a) the committed corpus carries N >= 10 scenarios, AND
#   (b) the committed control-arm fixture pair has graded both directions on every pull
#       request across >= 3 released versions.
# Both are readable from the tree and the tag history. Graduation is an OPERATOR
# decision at that point, never an automatic promotion by hit count.
#
# Ships DORMANT (warn) during the shakedown, per the warn-mode-initial posture. Note
# what is NOT governed by this token: the tag-filter assertion and the falsification arm
# fail the job outright in either mode. Those assert the gate's own machinery rather
# than the corpus's state, and a gate that is wrong about itself should be loud on day
# one.
warn
